# Vulnerabilities govulncheck reports against gwlint that we cannot currently
# act on, one ID per line. `mise run vulncheck` fails on anything reported that
# is not listed here, and also fails on an entry here that is no longer
# reported, so this file cannot quietly rot.
#
# Everything below reaches gwlint only through the package init() of code
# linked in transitively by kube-linter's lintcontext:
#
#   pkg/command/lint -> kube-linter/pkg/lintcontext -> k8s-manifests-lib
#     -> helm.sh/helm/v3/pkg/registry -> containerd/remotes
#
# gwlint verifies no signatures and talks to no container runtime, so none of
# these sit on a path gwlint's own code drives. Re-check each on every
# kube-linter or helm upgrade.

# golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained and unsafe by design. No CVE
# alias and no fix: the package is deprecated outright, not patched. Reached
# via helm's provenance verification, which gwlint never invokes.
GO-2026-5932

# The three below are CVE-2026-53492, CVE-2026-50195 and CVE-2026-53489, all
# fixed in containerd 2.1.9 / 2.2.5 / 2.3.2 and not backported to the 1.7 line.
# Those fixes are on the github.com/containerd/containerd/v2 module path, which
# minimum version selection cannot reach from the v1 path we are on: helm
# v3.20.0 requires github.com/containerd/containerd v1.7.x, and go.mod pins helm
# to v3.20.0 to match kube-linter v0.8.3 (see "A note on dependency versions" in
# the README). We track containerd 1.7.35, the newest of that line.
#
# The real blocker is helm, not containerd. These three come off the allowlist
# when helm moves to containerd v2 and the pin can follow.

# containerd CRI checkpoint restore: CDI annotation smuggling (CVE-2026-53492).
GO-2026-5064

# containerd CRI checkpoint import: local image tag poisoning (CVE-2026-50195).
GO-2026-5338

# containerd CRI checkpoint restore: arbitrary host CRI log file read via
# symlink following (CVE-2026-53489).
GO-2026-5622
